## Work

Wrote `dashboard/__tests__/storytime-print-student-book-adversarial-r2.test.ts` (220 insertions, 1 file). The file holds 10 test blocks and 49 test cases. All 49 pass on the current HEAD.

The split by area:

- Strict QR rule unit probes: 43 cases in 3 blocks (36 reject, 6 accept, 1 error-names-path).
- Caller integration: 6 cases in 6 blocks (3 build-stop rejects, 1 good-path print, 2 absent-URL renders).

No guard repeats R48 (dot segments, range edges 0 and 5 and 0 and 33, leading zeros, trailing space tab newline, fragment, wrong query key, unknown part value, doubled query, upper-case part value) or round 1 (full URL, protocol-relative URL, wrong prefix and case, leading space, wrong locale, empty path).

### Strict QR rule (43 cases)

- 8 percent-encoded forms throw: `%2e`, `%2F`, `%32`, `%31`, `%3F`, `%23`, `%73`, `%3Cscript%3E`.
- 3 non-ASCII digits throw: Devanagari, Arabic-Indic, full-width. The digit class matches ASCII only.
- 3 separators throw: CR, U+2028, NBSP.
- 2 backslash forms throw. 2 many-digit values throw (outside level 1 to 4 and week 1 to 32).
- 2 further range edges throw: 4/33 and 1/0.
- The trailing slash, the bare question mark, and the empty part throw.
- 5 near-miss part values and keys throw: `Book`, `songs`, `decodables`, `song `, `Part`.
- 4 valid-part-with-extra surroundings throw: `&x=1`, `x=1&`, `#frag`, `?x=1`.
- 2 interior spaces and 2 mixed-case routes throw.
- 6 good paths return host plus path byte-identical: 2/8, 4/1, 3/32, 3/17 with book, 4/32 with decodable, 1/32 with song.
- The error message names the rejected path.
- The accept blocks keep the reject blocks honest in both directions, so no guard passes vacuously.

### Caller integration (6 cases)

- An encoded song path stops the build with the hostile path in the message.
- A non-ASCII read-along path stops the build with the hostile path in the message.
- An empty part in the song path stops the build.
- A good non-shipped path prints the exact canonical address with a QR module grid.
- An absent read-along path prints exactly one code with the shipped song address (B-P2-09 behavior, now pinned).
- Absent both paths print no code and the leaf still renders.

